ted":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"**Describe the bug**\r\nThe AppImage generated by the bundler does not run. In particular, it yields the error \"cannot execute binary file: Exec format error\".\r\n\r\nI have managed to fix this by changing the `build_appimage` script in `src-tauri/target/release/bundle/appimage` to download an AppImage runtime and appending it to the image. In this case, the AppImage bundle successfully executes, but in the next execution of \r\n`yarn tauri:build ` the script `build_appimage` is overwritten.\r\n\r\n**To Reproduce**\r\n(This is based on a project created using `vue-cli-plugin-tauri`)\r\nSteps to reproduce the behaviour:\r\n1. Create new project using\r\n```\r\nvue create my-tauri-app\r\ncd my-tauri-app\r\nvue add tauri\r\n```\r\n2. Run `yarn tauri:build`\r\n3. Go to `src-tauri/target/release/bundle/appimage`\r\n4. Run `./app.AppImage\r\n\r\n**Expected behavior**\r\nRunning the AppImage should create a window with the default vue application.\r\n\r\n**Platform and Versions (please complete the following information):**\r\nOS:Linux(5.6.12-1-MANJARO) - linux/x64\r\nNode:14.1.0\r\nNPM:6.14.4\r\nYarn:1.22.4\r\nRustc:1.43.1\r\n\r\n**Additional context**\r\nThe appimage runtime I have used is https://github.com/AppImage/AppImageKit/releases/download/continuous/runtime-x86_64\r\n","closed_by":{"login":"lucasfernog","id":20051258,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwMDUxMjU4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/20051258?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lucasfernog","html_url":"https://github.com/lucasfernog","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lucasfernog/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lucasfernog/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lucasfernog/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lucasfernog/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subsc